Z||000000||jeffndebrus||11-22-2001||12:35 PM||||<P><BR>Road Warriors | GM FWD Links || Credits | KW's Z26 | Guestbook | New | Home |<BR>Site Information | Beretta's Only | Performance Parts Info | FWD SnapShots | Message Board | Makes & Models<P><BR>Makes & Models<P>Note: the following is a compilation of GM's FWD makes and models, starting with the late-70's/early-80's X-platform. This list is organized by platform, with the various makes/models listed within each platform. Each model will include production runs, engines, and trim level designations. I'm still incorporating a lot of information into the list, it is nowhere near complete. Any information regarding errors or additions to this section is greatly appreciated!<P>See bottom of page for engine notes...<P>Special thanks to E Man, Tyler Grant and Jim Butler of BerettaNet for their help in getting this started! Also, thanks to Wayne Bengston Jr., Kris Hulteen, Carey and everyone else who e-mailed me with useful information regarding this section. I appreciate it. <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<P>A-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Chevrolet Celebrity 1982-90 CL, Eurosport, VR 2.5 four, 2.8 V6, 3.1 V6, 4.3 D V6  <BR>Oldsmobile Cutlass Ciera<BR>(Cutlass Cruiser Wagon) 1982-97 S, SE, GT, Brougham, Series 1 & 2 2.2 four, 2.5 four, 3.0 V6, 3.1 V6, 3.3 V6, 3.8 V6, 4.3 D V6 <BR>Pontiac 6000 1982-91 LE, SE, STE 2.5 four, 3.1 V6, 4.3 D V6 <BR>Buick Century 1982-95 Special, Custom, Limited 2.2 four, 3.1 V6, 3.3 V6, 3.8 V6, 4.3 D V6 <P>C-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Buick Park Avenue  Ultra  <BR>Cadillac Deville 1985-1994   <BR>Oldsmobile 98 Regency 1986-89 Series I & II  <P>E-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Oldsmobile Toronado   3.8 V6 <BR>Buick Reatta   3.8 V6 <BR>Buick Riviera 1993-95   <BR>Cadillac Eldorado  ETC 4.6 DOHC V8, 4.9 V8 <P>G-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Oldsmobile Aurora 1995-present  4.0 DOHC V8 <BR>Buick Riviera 1995-99  3.8 V6 (NA or SC) <P>H-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Oldsmobile Delta 88  LS, LSS, Royale 3.0 V6, 3.8 V6 (NA or SC) <BR>Pontiac Bonneville 1987-present SE, SSE, SLE, SSEi 3.0 V6, 3.8 V6 (NA or SC) <BR>Buick LeSabre 1986-present Custom, Limited, T-Type 3.0 V6, 3.8 V6 (NA or SC) <P>J-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Chevrolet Cavalier 1982-present Type-10, CL, VL, RS, LS, Z24 2.0/2.2 four, 2.3/2.4 DOHC four, 2.8/3.1 V6 <BR>Pontiac Sunbird 1984-94 LE, SE, GT 2.0 SOHC (T), 3.1 V6 <BR>Pontiac Sunfire 1995-present SE, GT 2.2 four, 2.3/2.4 DOHC four <BR>Pontiac J2000 1982-83  1.8 SOHC (T) <BR>Cadillac Cimarron 1982-88  2.8 V6 <BR>Oldsmobile Firenza 1982-89 GT  <BR>Buick Skyhawk 1982-89 T-Type 1.8 SOHC (T), 2.0 OHV, 2.0 SOHC (T) <P>K-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Cadillac Seville 1992- SLS, STS 4.9 V8, 4.6 DOHC V8 <BR>Cadillac Deville 1994- Concours 4.6 DOHC V8 <P>L-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Chevrolet Beretta 1987-96 GT, GTZ, GTU, Z26, Indy 2.0/2.2 four, 2.3 DOHC four, 2.8/3.1 V6 <BR>Chevrolet Corsica 1987-96 LT, LTZ, XT 2.0/2.2 four, 2.8/3.1 V6 <BR>Pontiac Tempest<BR>(Canadien model) 1987-92 LE 2.0/2.2 four, 2.8/3.1 V6 <P>N-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Pontiac Grand Am 1985-present LE, SE, GT 2.0 T four, 2.5 four, 2.3/2.4 SOHC/DOHC four, 3.0 V6, 3.1 V6, 3.4 V6, 3.3 V6 <BR>Chevrolet Malibu 1997-present LS 2.4 DOHC four, 3.1 V6 <BR>Buick Skylark 1986-96 Custom, Limited, GS 2.4 four, 3.0 V6, 3.1 V6, 3.3 V6 <BR>Buick Somerset 1985-87  2.5 I4, 3.0 V6 <BR>Oldsmobile Cutlass Calais 1985-91 GT, 442, W41 3.0 V6, 2.3 DOHC four <BR>Oldsmobile Achieva 1992-97 SL, SC, SCX, Series I-III 2.3 DOHC four, 3.1 V6, 3.3 V6 <BR>Oldsmobile Cutlass 1997-99 GL, GLS 2.4 DOHC four, 3.1 V6 <BR>Oldsmobile Alero 1999-present GX, GL, GLS 2.4 DOHC four, 3.4 V6 <P>V-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Cadillac Allante   4.1 V8, 4.6 DOHC V8, 4.9 V8 <BR>Buick Reatta   3.8 V6 <P>W-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Pontiac Grand Prix 1988-present LE, SE, STE, GT, TGP, GTP 2.3 DOHC four, 2.8/3.1 V6, 3.1 V6 (T), 3.4 V6, 3.4 DOHC V6, 3.8 V6 (NA or SC) <BR>Buick Regal 1988-present Custom, Limited, GS, T-type 2.8/3.1 V6, 3.8 V6 (NA or SC) <BR>Chevrolet Lumina 1990-present Eurosport, LS, LTZ, Z34 2.2 four, 2.5 four, 3.1 V6, 3.4 DOHC V6, 3.8 V6 <BR>Chevrolet Monte Carlo 1995-present LS, Z34, SS 3.1 V6, 3.4 DOHC V6, 3.4 V6, 3.8 V6 <BR>Chevrolet Impala 2000-present LS 3.4 V6, 3.8 V6 <BR>Oldsmobile Cutlass Supreme 1990-97 S, SL, International, Series I-IV 2.3 DOHC four, 3.1 V6, 3.4 DOHC V6 <BR>Oldsmobile Cutlass 1988-89   <BR>Oldsmobile Intrigue 1998-present GX, GL, GLS 3.5 DOHC V6, 3.8 V6 <P>X-Body Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Chevrolet Citation 1980-85 XS, X-11 2.5 I4, 2.8 V6 <BR>Buick Skylark 1980-85  2.8 V6 <BR>Pontiac Phoenix 1980-84  2.5 I4, 2.8 V6 <BR>Oldsmobile Omega 1980-84  2.8 V6 <P>Z-Body (Saturn) Platform <BR>Make & Model Production Years Trim Levels Engines <BR>Sedan 1990-present SL1, SL2 1.9 four (SOHC or DOHC) <BR>Coupe 1990-present SC1, SC2 1.9 four (SOHC or DOHC) <BR>Wagon 1990-present SW1, SW2 1.9 four (SOHC or DOHC) <P>Engines <BR>Displacement (liters) Type Horsepower Notes <BR>1.8 OHV I4   <BR>1.8 OHC T I4 150hp  <BR>1.9 SOHC/DOHC I4 90/124hp Exclusive to Saturns. <BR>2.0 OHV TBI I4 90hp  <BR>2.0 OHC T I4 160hp Enlarged version of 1.8 T engine. <BR>2.2 OHV TBI/MFI I4 90/120hp Reworked for MFI in '94. <BR>2.3 SOHC/DOHC I4 120/150/170/180/190hp Known as "Quad 4." Availble in several forms, including H.O. <BR>2.4 DOHC 150hp Revised Quad 4, renamed "Twin Cam." Big change was addition of balance shafts for smoothness. <BR>2.5 OHV TBI I4 92/98/110/120hp Nick-named the "Iron Duke." <BR>2.8 OHV 60-degree carb/MFI V6 112/120/125/130/135hp There was a H.O. (135hp) carb version available in some A-bodies. <BR>3.0 OHV 90-degree V6   <BR>3.0 DOHC V6 hp Exclusive to Saturn L-series. <BR>3.1 OHV 60-degree MFI V6 140/160hp Enlarged version of 2.8 MFI V6. There was a turbo version in a few 89-90 Grand Prix's. <BR>3.1 OHV 60-degree SFI V6 150/155/160/170/175hp Significantly reworked version of 3.1 MFI V6. Power was bumped up in the 2K model year with some intake revisions. <BR>3.3 OHV 90-degree V6 160hp  <BR>3.4 OHV 60-degree SFI V6 170/175/180hp Enlarged version of 3.1 SFI V6. New Pontiac GA has 175hp Ram Air version. <BR>3.4 DOHC 60-degree V6 210/215hp  <BR>3.5 DOHC V6 215hp This is the all-new Olds Intrigue engine. Based off the Northstar V8. Expected to eventually replace 3.8 V6 throughout GM's lineup. <BR>3.8 90-degree OHV V6 150/170/200/240hp There are so many forms of this engine, I can't keep track! Available supercharged. <BR>4.0 DOHC V8 250hp A form of the Northstar V8. Used in the Olds Aurora. <BR> 4.1 OHV V8 Cadillac engine. <BR>4.3 90-degree OHV D V6 85hp  <BR>4.5 OHV V8  Another Cadillac engine. <BR>4.6 DOHC V8 275/300hp Named "Northstar." Exclusive to FWD Cadillac's. <BR>4.9 V8  Another Cadillac-only engine (at least FWD). <BR>    <P><BR>Engine Abbreviations: H.O.=High Output, SC=supercharged, NA=normally aspirated, T=turbocharged, D=diesel, DOHC=dual overhead cam, SOHC=single overhead cam, OHV=overhead valve, I4=Inline 4 cylinder, MFI=multi-port fuel injection, SFI=sequential-port fuel injection, TBI=throttle body injection, carb=carbuerated fuel injection.<BR>FWD Makes & Models sold by GM (Made by other manufacturers)<BR>Geo Metro/Suzuki Swift<BR>Geo Prizm/Toyota Corolla(1989-)<BR>Geo Storm/Isuzu Impulse (1990-?)<BR>Chevrolet Sprint (1985-88)<BR>Chevrolet/Geo Spectrum<BR>Chevrolet Nova/Toyota Corolla (80's version)<BR>Pontiac Lemans (80's/90's version)<P>-------------